                <head><hi rendition="#bold">Paper Prepared in the National Security
                        Council</hi><anchor n="4" xml:id="d78-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian">undated</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">AGENDA</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">FOR</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">NSC
                        MEETING ON BUILD-DOWN</hi></p>
                <p>A. Introduction—Judge Clark</p>
                <p>B. Build-Down—All Principals</p>
                <p>Discussion of the basic approach and strategy implementing the build-down concept
                    outlined in the Senior Arms Control Policy Group discussion paper. Discussion
                    should focus on the following questions:</p>
                <p>1. What should be the Administration’s final position on implementing the
                    build-down concept? When and how should the full bottom-line be revealed?</p>
                <p>2. Given the current political environment, what should be the thrust and level
                    of detail of the Administration presentations made at Congressional hearings
                    scheduled for the week of September 12?</p>
                <p>3. What additional steps need the Administration be prepared to take prior to key
                    votes later in the month?</p>
            </div>
        </body>
